se effects across drug classes\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Multiple drugs are associated with neurological and GI disturbances. For example, 氟西汀 (fluoxetine) is linked to 言语障碍 (speech disorders) in combination with other antidepressants, presenting with confusion, hallucinations, and tremors. 二甲双胍 (metformin) commonly causes 胃胀 (bloating), along with diarrhea and abdominal discomfort. Similarly, voriconazole use correlates with upper abdominal symptoms and neuropsychiatric changes. These adverse effects, while often non-life-threatening, significantly impact patient quality of life and adherence, warranting proactive management and patient counseling. [Data: Relationships (12850, 8493, 8807)]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community presents a high impact severity due to the prevalence of serious, potentially life-threatening adverse drug reactions—particularly disulfiram-like reactions and respiratory/cardiac toxicities—linked to commonly used medications.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782128540, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1552, "prompt_tokens": 6754, "total_tokens": 8306, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 0}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"Adverse Drug Reaction Network: Focus on Disulfiram-like Reactions and Respiratory/Cardiovascular Symptoms\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on a network of drugs, symptoms, side effects, and populations linked through documented adverse drug reactions (ADRs) and contraindications. Key drugs include伏立康唑 (voriconazole), 头孢哌酮舒巴坦钠 (cefoperazone/sulbactam), 头孢孟多 (cefa